{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/151609-reflexive-actions","id":151609,"title":"Reflexive actions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-28T13:02:30-07:00","id":151609,"title":"Reflexive actions","content":"Starting a new thread because otherwise it'd be off-topic<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/150001-psychic-vampire-template?p=151576#post151576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this brings up the question of whether you can use reflexive healing outside your turn. Is it actually BP/PU per turn or per round? Can I heal 10L for 1 essence on each of my opponents 10 turns?<br /> <br /> That might be an important thing to address there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reflexive actions have been defined as &quot;breathing&quot; or &quot;walking&quot;. Can my character breathe while you're taking your turn? I'd think so. So I'd be inclined to say &quot;yes&quot; to that question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T13:23:05-07:00","id":151625,"title":"","content":"Characters can absolutely take reflexive actions during other character's actions. Otherwise things like Celerity's interrupt ability would be worthless, and the Demonic Form Teleportation feature wouldn't need to specify that it can only be used during your action.<br /> <br /> However, an opponent's action does not constitute the start of a new turn. Indeed that the thinking about turns is completely off. It helps not to think of turns as individual characters taking actions in orderly an orderly sequential manner, then waiting for other people to take theirs. This isn't Final Fantasy or Disgaea. Everyone is acting simultaneously, in one flowing blur of motion. The initiative order is merely an abstraction for the sake of ease.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T13:40:50-07:00","id":151642,"title":"","content":"Well, guess that means that if you don't kill a high PU werewolf completely in one swing, its going to be a long fight =P Sounds fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T13:49:50-07:00","id":151653,"title":"","content":"Or you need to bring Agg damage to the fight as the primary way to combat the high healing rates of powerful vampires and werewolves.<br /> <br /> But this has been settled since the original nWOD core book. The game term &quot;turn&quot; is not an individual character's action during combat, but rather one full cycle of the initiative roster. If you can heal 5L in a turn, it is always 5L in a turn, not 5L per chance to act for every character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T23:17:49-07:00","id":157555,"title":"","content":"It does bring up the problem of how reflexive actions interact with successive attempts, though. Say you have ten swords equipped, each with the magic property of teleporting it out of your hand and back home once drawn, thus negating any attacks. Would you be able to Quick Draw all ten in a single turn? Or simply draw and sheate one sword ten times in one turn? Per a strict reading of the rules, you would, but it seems unrealistic.<br /> <br /> It is a far fetched example to the point of making the whole thing seem like a non-issue, until you have to house-rule two instant actions taking place in the span of one turn, forcing you to make one of them reflexive, then wondering what is to stop the character from spamming it, with precedent from reflexive Resistance efforts that seems to increase the amount of effort a character is capable of in proportion to how many enemies are faced in a turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making Star Wars WoD conversion. Gonna be done when it's done. Hopefully not too long now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2217-darthmrn","name":"DarthMRN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T00:21:08-07:00","id":157593,"title":"","content":"Unless drawing/sheathing/holstering a weapon has some specific effect that doesn't end combat... being able to draw and holster it lots of times is generally meaningless. Sure, the GMC rules are written such that you could do this, but when is it actually going to happen?<br /> <br /> Yes, any house rules that deal with reflexive actions have to consider the possibility of spam... but that's easy. Just because something is reflexive doesn't mean that you can do it more than once a turn. Just say, &quot;this is reflexive, but can only be used once in a turn,&quot; like spending WP. Or you could scale it like spending blood points is only one use per turn doesn't seem right (like you can Quick Draw Wits - 2 times per turn).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T00:38:43-07:00","id":157606,"title":"","content":"I'm admittedly way behind on my Vampire, but isn't this very thread proof that it is a consideration even in regular games, with reflexive vampiric healing potentially using Resistance precedent to increase healing proportional to how many people participate in a fight? From what you say, the devs had to go out and clarify it back in the day, so maybe they should have included it in GMC too.<br /> <br /> But yes, I agree with the limitations. I just happen to dislike cases where the RAW permits various kinds of abuse, cause it sets a negative precedent for houserules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making Star Wars WoD conversion. Gonna be done when it's done. Hopefully not too long now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2217-darthmrn","name":"DarthMRN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T01:53:34-07:00","id":157662,"title":"","content":"There's no issue with how healing worked, or works now. You can heal per turn, not per action, based on your Blood Potency. If you can spend 2 vitae a turn, then that's all the healing you can get. It doesn't matter how many opponents you fight because how many opponents you fight doesn't change the refresh rate of a turn.<br /> <br /> This has, literally, never been an issue. There are rules where the number of reflexive actions aren't capped that can cause problems (the GMC Quick Draw as written, for example), but anything that says, &quot;per turn,&quot; is not subject to the number of opponents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T09:37:04-07:00","id":157964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarthMRN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/151609-reflexive-actions?p=157606#post157606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm admittedly way behind on my Vampire, but isn't this very thread proof that it is a consideration even in regular games, with reflexive vampiric healing potentially using Resistance precedent to increase healing proportional to how many people participate in a fight? From what you say, the devs had to go out and clarify it back in the day, so maybe they should have included it in GMC too.<br /> <br /> But yes, I agree with the limitations. I just happen to dislike cases where the RAW permits various kinds of abuse, cause it sets a negative precedent for houserules.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't healing proportional to number of opponents. Its healing by round, not turn. Instead of vitae/turn, its more appropriate to say vitae/round.<br /> <br /> My mention of werewolves and healing for each opponent was an example of a PU 10 werewolf using 1 essence per opponent and never going over his turn/round limit.<br /> <br /> I think you misunderstood. In Idigam chronicles, the amount of lethal healed per essence is based on Primal urge, which also determines how many essence you can spend. That 100 healing was still just 10 essence in theory. It never went over the limit of per turn, but I could see that it could be confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T12:41:35-07:00","id":158112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/151609-reflexive-actions?p=157964#post157964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its healing by round, not turn. Instead of vitae/turn, its more appropriate to say vitae/round.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no such thing as &quot;rounds&quot; in the nWOD combat system. Really.<br /> <br /> &quot;Turn&quot; in the system is not &quot;my character's turn to act&quot; but &quot;one full turn of the Initiative roster.&quot; The system defines &quot;turn,&quot; &quot;initiative,&quot; and &quot;actions.&quot; Never &quot;rounds.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T13:39:15-07:00","id":158223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/151609-reflexive-actions?p=158112#post158112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no such thing as &quot;rounds&quot; in the nWOD combat system. Really.<br /> <br /> &quot;Turn&quot; in the system is not &quot;my character's turn to act&quot; but &quot;one full turn of the Initiative roster.&quot; The system defines &quot;turn,&quot; &quot;initiative,&quot; and &quot;actions.&quot; Never &quot;rounds.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Same thing, your just nitpicking. More people will understand the difference if phrased as a round in this regard as generally a turn is most understood as your turn in the initiative roster, rather than a full run of said initiative roster.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't recall actually seeing it say that, ever. Sure rounds aren't mentioned, but it doesn't say a turn is a &quot;full turn of the initiative roster&quot;. What I did find was:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WoD core pg 121</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Turn\u2014The smallest increment, and often the most<br /> important, a turn is three seconds. It\u2019s the amount of time<br /> it takes a character to perform a quick action, called an<br /> instant action (see p. 126). Turns are mainly observed in<br /> combat, when the action is fast and furious, with all characters<br /> doing something dramatic in a short timeframe.</div> </div> </div> </div>And<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>B&amp;S pg 173</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Turn \u2014 The smallest increment of time, a turn lasts for about<br /> three seconds. A character can perform a single instant action<br /> in a turn. Turns normally only matter in combat or other<br /> dramatic and stressful situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>We all know your knowledgeable about the system. But there is no need to be nitpicky when something expressed is rather clear and makes it more obvious. I recognize that rounds aren't explicitly called out, but it is also a common term that is reflected in most tabletop games.<br /> <br /> More people understand what a round is than will understand that a turn accounts for all turns in the roster.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T17:57:26-07:00","id":158462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/151609-reflexive-actions?p=158223#post158223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same thing, your just nitpicking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then what, exactly, is the point of saying that it should be phrased as &quot;vitae/round&quot; instead of &quot;vitae/turn,&quot; if you acknowledge that they're the same thing?<br /> <br /> You said, &quot;Its healing by round, not turn.&quot; And now you're complaining that I'm nitpicking because &quot;rounds and &quot;turns&quot; are the same thing... but your statement only makes sense if you're contending that they are not the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More people will understand the difference if phrased as a round in this regard as generally a turn is most understood as your turn in the initiative roster, rather than a full run of said initiative roster. </div> </div> </div>If people don't read the rules, they aren't going to understand the rules. This is not a common thing people have asked about since the nWOD came out that I have seen (and the phrasing hasn't changed significantly). I have yet to meet anyone that doesn't get what a &quot;turn&quot; means in the nWOD system either from reading the book, or asking for clarification. It isn't hard.<br /> <br /> The rules are not terribly ambiguous on this point. You just cited them. Though you should add nWOD core's pages 150-151, specifically on 150 under the header of &quot;Combat Turns.&quot; Since that's pretty important to understanding how the system defines combat turns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I recognize that rounds aren't explicitly called out, but it is also a common term that is reflected in most tabletop games. </div> </div> </div>Every game uses different terminology. Often the same words to mean slightly different but related things. Some games use one term and others don't use it. In the end, it doesn't matter what a group of possible people might be more used to defining a given term as; they need to read the rules of the new game and understand how it uses its own terminology.<br /> <br /> And if we want to make assumptions about what &quot;most people&quot; will understand, or what is common understanding, then we can assume that most people would understand that &quot;once per turn&quot; does not mean, &quot;once per every action every character in the fight takes,&quot; since most people are going to assume it is, &quot;once per my action,&quot; if they aren't going to realize the specifics of the rules. Because that's how games tend to work.<br /> <br /> And if something seems funky and they go back and read the rules in more depth to try to figure out why.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More people understand what a round is than will understand that a turn accounts for all turns in the roster. </div> </div> </div>Who is the group of people we're using to start picking out this majority from anyway? More people have never played a RPG and if they're reading the nWOD as their first one, aren't going to have any preconceptions that would lead to your assessment. Most people that have played a RPG will have either been expose to the fact that they tend to have a lot of rules and reading them carefully (or having someone you trust to know them accurately) is important, or have played very rule-light games and suddenly see a ton of rules to read through... and probably find it important to read them (if they don't stop reading because they find it too many rules for their tastes).<br /> <br /> And, again, a turn does not account &quot;for all turns&quot; in the roster; but rather all actions taken during the roster. The books don't phrase it that way because that's clearly confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T18:24:48-07:00","id":158506,"title":"","content":"Are you just trying to pick a fight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T20:56:53-07:00","id":158636,"title":"","content":"No. I'm:<br /> <br /> 1) Pointing out that insisting on calling actions &quot;turns,&quot; and combat turns &quot;rounds,&quot; does nothing to make things more clear as the book defines these things adequately.<br /> <br /> 2) Pointing out that you're making massive assumptions about how closely people bother reading the rules, what experience people have with RPGs to have preconceptions about the definitions of terms but not preconceptions about needing to learn each game's specific definitions.<br /> <br /> 3) Responding poorly to being dismissed as &quot;nitpicking&quot; and what not in a discussion where you're complaint is purely semantic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T21:11:06-07:00","id":158678,"title":"","content":"&quot;Round&quot; is a common colloquial term for a full initiative rotation of actions taken in combat, colloquially referred to as &quot;turns&quot;. The nWoD rules use the term &quot;turn&quot; to mean the former, and &quot;action&quot; to mean the latter, but they describe the same concepts. The important thing to remember is that &quot;per turn&quot; limits apply to the full rotation of combat actions, not to each individual action within that rotation. Call it what you like, just know what the game means when it uses the word &quot;turn&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T18:24:04-07:00","id":160434,"title":"","content":"For what it is worth, given that turn is used to mean two different things, the use of round for the purposes of explanation *was* helpful in reminding me how vampire healing works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making Star Wars WoD conversion. Gonna be done when it's done. Hopefully not too long now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2217-darthmrn","name":"DarthMRN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T00:01:03-07:00","id":160619,"title":"","content":"Turn, in the rules, is not used to mean two different things. It means one thing (the amount of time in which you can take a single instant action) and in combat where you have lots of characters acting in a single turn, you organize all those actions using the Initiative rules. Turn is not used in any other way by the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T17:16:08-07:00","id":1085236,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the necro - but the thread seems appropriate Just a question that I figured I'd address because...honestly, I don't know and really couldn't find a straight answer in any of the books. Can you take like multiple reflexive actions at once? Let's say for my turn in the initiative order I want to move and strike an opponent. If I'm playing an Uratha and I want to use Beserker's Might, Slaughterer, and Primal Strength. If I have the necessary level of Primal Urge let's say like 7 for simplicity sake and pay the necessary essence; can I do it?<br /> <br /> Basically - can multiple reflexive actions be taken in the same turn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T17:39:47-07:00","id":1085245,"title":"","content":"Yes. Unless something in the specific rules of a reflexive action make it incompatible with other reflexive actions, or some other system constraints (like spending points), would stop you, you can use multiple reflexive actions in the same turn.<br /> <br /> So if you have the points, you can toss on a bunch of reflexive powers at once. High power stat supernaturals are scary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T18:13:33-07:00","id":1085258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/151609-reflexive-actions?p=1085245#post1085245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Unless something in the specific rules of a reflexive action make it incompatible with other reflexive actions, or some other system constraints (like spending points), would stop you, you can use multiple reflexive actions in the same turn.<br /> <br /> So if you have the points, you can toss on a bunch of reflexive powers at once. High power stat supernaturals are scary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sheesh , well glad I know for certain, Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . (Also what do you mean like spending points? - lost me with this part of it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T18:59:43-07:00","id":1085272,"title":"","content":"By spending points, I mean the reason you used a Primal Urge 7 example character. A Primal Urge 1 character that can only spend 1 Essence per turn can't activate a bunch of Essence costing reflexive powers a turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T16:11:39-07:00","id":1085931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/151609-reflexive-actions?p=1085236#post1085236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the necro - but the thread seems appropriate Just a question that I figured I'd address because...honestly, I don't know and really couldn't find a straight answer in any of the books. Can you take like multiple reflexive actions at once? Let's say for my turn in the initiative order I want to move and strike an opponent. If I'm playing an Uratha and I want to use Beserker's Might, Slaughterer, and Primal Strength. If I have the necessary level of Primal Urge let's say like 7 for simplicity sake and pay the necessary essence; can I do it?<br /> <br /> Basically - can multiple reflexive actions be taken in the same turn?</div> </div> </div> </div>How many times do you breath in a turn? More than once? How many steps can you take in a turn? More than one? Those are reflexive actions as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T17:22:12-07:00","id":1085954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/151609-reflexive-actions?p=1085931#post1085931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How many times do you breath in a turn? More than once? How many steps can you take in a turn? More than one? Those are reflexive actions as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I meant more significant things you know? Like using a Werewolf Gift or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T16:52:13-07:00","id":1086383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/151609-reflexive-actions?p=1085954#post1085954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I meant more significant things you know? Like using a Werewolf Gift or the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reflexive actions are reflexive. The act of spending essence, willpower, or rolling to resist some supernatural power are all reflexive as well, meaning they don't penalize your turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}